modules.lesson:
CSS variables, also known as custom properties, are a powerful way to manage design tokens like colors, spacing, and typography across your entire application. By defining these variables in the :root pseudo-class, you create a single source of truth that makes theme management and dark mode implementation significantly easier. Instead of hardcoding hex values everywhere, you can simply reference the variable, allowing you to update your entire site's look by changing just one line of code.

For example, you can define a primary color and use it in multiple places: 
:root { --primary-color: #3498db; } 
.button { background-color: var(--primary-color); }

